#: src/reference/lints.md:56
msgid "Checks if `hint-mostly-unused` being applied to all dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:58 src/reference/lints.md:95
#: src/reference/lints.md:143 src/reference/lints.md:184
#: src/reference/lints.md:221 src/reference/lints.md:254
#: src/reference/lints.md:287 src/reference/lints.md:320
#: src/reference/lints.md:356 src/reference/lints.md:393
#: src/reference/lints.md:428 src/reference/lints.md:449
#: src/reference/lints.md:469 src/reference/lints.md:493
#: src/reference/lints.md:546 src/reference/lints.md:568
msgid "Why it is bad"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:59
msgid ""
"`hint-mostly-unused` indicates that most of a crate's API surface will go "
"unused by anything depending on it; this hint can speed up the build by "
"attempting to minimize compilation time for items that aren't used at all. "
"Misapplication to crates that don't fit that criteria will slow down the "
"build rather than speeding it up. It should be selectively applied to "
"dependencies that meet these criteria. Applying it globally is always a "
"misapplication and will likely slow down the build."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:67 src/reference/lints.md:117
#: src/reference/lints.md:149 src/reference/lints.md:196
#: src/reference/lints.md:229 src/reference/lints.md:262
#: src/reference/lints.md:295 src/reference/lints.md:328
#: src/reference/lints.md:362 src/reference/lints.md:401
#: src/reference/lints.md:475 src/reference/lints.md:518
#: src/reference/lints.md:549 src/reference/lints.md:571
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:68
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[profile.dev.package.\"*\"]\n"
"hint-mostly-unused = true\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

